# ── Chapter 3 fidelity pins: "Who Holds the Pen" ─────────────────────────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/03-who-holds-the-pen.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # the real check — the line above cannot see
#                        # the cross-file reconciliation or the prose guards

:expect-pins 20

# "The electorate seated you. You have not been recalled. And you were not
#  voided in an earlier period." — all three holding gives the pen.
? choose(Electorate, Gia).
# => TRUE

? permits(Review, Gia).
# => TRUE

? permits(Tribunal, Wren).
# => TRUE

# "Writing it down directly is not forbidden-and-punished; it is refused."
:refuse reasoning /declared derived-only/
permits(Review, Sock).

# "Boss keeps standing permanently and loses the credential immediately."
? choose(Electorate, Boss).
# => TRUE

? broken(Boss).
# => TRUE

? authority(Boss).
# => TRUE

? permits(Review, Boss).
# => FALSE

# "Vex was also seated, and was never recalled — but Vex was voided in an
#  earlier period. Vex has no pen either."
? choose(Electorate, Vex).
# => TRUE

? rotten(Vex).
# => TRUE

? permits(Review, Vex).
# => FALSE

# "On the account so far, Nia should be a prisoner — the injury, the judgment,
# the machinery." The premises are pinned so the relief verdict below cannot go
# vacuous: prisoner(Nia) FALSE means something only while a conviction is there
# to be relieved.
? injure(Nia, Ivo).
# => TRUE

? judge(Court, Nia).
# => TRUE

# "Nia is not a prisoner, because Nia was cleared."
? clear(Nia).
# => TRUE

# [v0.9] ...and the adjudication the relief now requires
? judge(Appeals, Nia).
# => TRUE

? permits(Appeals, Nia).
# => TRUE

? prisoner(Nia).
# => FALSE

# ── THE BARE FLAG DERIVES NOTHING. Ground fact persists; keep this last ──────
# "The entry that says you are in the clear still names nobody. The judgment
# it must accompany names the body that made it." Adam — convicted, homeless,
# housed by confinement — is written as cleared, with no examination anywhere
# near the word, and nothing moves. Negative-controlled against the pre-guard
# constitution: these three flip (the flag alone sprang him), and Nia's pins
# above stand either way.
clear(Adam).

? permits(Appeals, Adam).
# => FALSE

? prisoner(Adam).
# => TRUE

? travel(Adam).
# => FALSE
